@nsobid-891687F016A18F1773D4A88EBF8A973C8E33ECC1

# Super Mario 3D World + Bowser's Fury [010028600EBDA000] (base game, main NSO build id above; XCI boots with "Update v0.0.0" = v1.0.0)
# 4:3 Aspect Ratio + HUD fit - RomCore. Eden handheld mode (guest 16:9 picture), RomCore stretches the picture 4/3 vertically.
#
# 1) 0040B818 (code 0x40b918): swapchain/render size 1920x1080 -> 960x720 (mov x28,#0x3c0 ; movk x28,#0x2d0,lsl #32).
# 2) 00738678 -> cave 009C4D00: sead PerspectiveProjection::set() (0x738720) stores its aspect at [obj+0xb0]; when the value is ~16/9
#    it is replaced by 4/3 (vertical FOV unchanged). Only set() is patched: the ui2d layout renderer builds its own projection through
#    the ctor (0x738640, called from 0x9702dc) and must keep 16:9 or the HUD gets stretched sideways.
# 3) 0069D120 -> cave 009C4A80: hook at the entry of nn::ui2d::Pane::CalculateMtx (0x69d220), runs the original and then post-processes:
#    - root pane (no parent, height 680..1000, i.e. the 1280x720 layouts): height := 960, Y scale := 0.75 (undistorted after the host's 4/3 stretch)
#    - full-screen panes (width >= 1200, height 690..760) inside such a layout: height := 960, width x4/3 (cover-crop for backgrounds/art)
#    - top/bottom anchoring: a pane whose parent is near the layout centre (|y| < 108) and whose own world |y| is large is moved outward by
#      up to 90 units (ramp 60..210), so edge-anchored HUD stays on the real screen edges. Panes named "Base" are left alone (char-select).
# Caves live in the zero padding at the end of .text (image 0x9c4a80..0x9c4fff).

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

@enabled
